From 64f4cd8fcb2ccaed201dfcdde4234758927cb015 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 08:18:58 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat(vulkan): MMVQ A-side decode hoist behind spec constant
 (R48b)

The MMVQ mat-vec nest re-runs the entire weight decode inside the column
loop: mmvq_dot_product() does repack4() plus the scale reads before it
touches a B word, and neither of its arguments depends on the column, so
the decode is repeated NUM_COLS times per (row, k-slice).

Split every type arm of mul_mat_vecq_funcs.glsl into mmvq_load_a() (the A
decode) and mmvq_dot_a() (the dots against the cached B block plus the
scale apply); mmvq_dot_product() is now their composition, so the
inherited entry point is unchanged. iter() gains a second nest behind
specialization constant 3 that decodes A once per row per k-slice into
registers and then loops the columns doing only the B load and the dot.

Both nests call the same pair in the same order, so results are
bit-identical by construction. The shader default is 0 (inherited nest);
the host probes ON for AMD and OFF elsewhere, GGML_ARIFI_MMVQ_A_HOIST
overrides in both directions on one binary, IQ1_S/IQ1_M are gated off by
default on register grounds and move with GGML_ARIFI_MMVQ_A_HOIST_IQ1.
NUM_COLS == 1 folds to the inherited nest at pipeline-compile time.

Correctness only. test-backend-ops MUL_MAT on Vulkan0 under
GGML_VK_FORCE_MMVQ=1: q4_K 71/71 and sx8 108/108, in both the probe-ON
and the forced-OFF arm, 0 FAIL. No perf run; the ON-vs-OFF pairing and
the planted reds are owed to HQ.

Origin: fork-authored (ArifiLabs lane-235 R48b MMVQ A-hoist, Opus 5 MEDIUM kernel-maker)
Measured-effect: UNMEASURED - correctness only; pairing owed to HQ chain134
Lane: lane-235
Conflict-resolved: S6 strict auto_merge - wrap/same-point regions merged in place (fixS6_605.py)
